            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="WHE05" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Charles</forename>
                        <surname>Wheatstone</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1802">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1875"/>
                    <occupation>inventor and scientist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Possibly Charles Wheatstone - an instrument maker, turned scientist,
                            later knighted. Wheatsen and Wheatson, seem to be Godwin's early
                            encounters - where he clearly has not grasped the spelling of the name
                            (and its pronunication might well have been Wheatsen). The
                            continuity between the Wheatsen entriees and the later Wheatstone ones - in
                            terms of the circles in which he appears, around Martin and Pickering, make this unlikely to
                            be coincidental and suggest these are the same person.</p>
                    </note>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
